# Security descriptor applied to every sudoRole object created from this
# class.  Without it the objects inherit an SD with no Authenticated Users
# read ACE, so domain member machine accounts -- which is what SSSD binds as
# -- cannot read them.  The rules are then invisible to every client:
# `Received 0 sudo rules` in the backend log and `sudo -l` permanently empty,
# while the rule is plainly there when inspected with ldbsearch as root on
# the DC (root bypasses ACLs, which is what made this so hard to see).
# (A;;RPLCLORC;;;AU) is the read grant AD's own stock classes carry.
defaultSecurityDescriptor: D:(A;;RPWPCRCCDCLCLORCWOWDSDDTSW;;;DA)(A;;RPWPCRCCDCLCLORCWOWDSDDTSW;;;EA)(A;;RPWPCRCCDCLCLORCWOWDSDDTSW;;;SY)(A;;RPLCLORC;;;AU)
